### Summary

Knowledge returns navigation links and backlinks for a wikilink inside inert image alt text, although its shared renderer emits no anchor and its editable-link scanner returns no link.

### Steps to reproduce

In a disposable source checkout at `f6abc882721d0facb24452469b77cf58b95d25a7` with frozen repository dependencies prepared, save the standalone fixture below as `extensions/knowledge/src/public-image-link-proof.test.ts` and run:

```sh
node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/knowledge/src/public-image-link-proof.test.ts --maxWorkers=1
```

The fixture uses actual registered `knowledge_save_page`, `knowledge_record`, and `knowledge_connections` tools with a native disposable store. It creates a fictional target, an unrelated target, a changing note, and an always-visible navigation control. The changing note goes from image-alt text to a visible wikilink and back.

### Expected behavior

`![Caption [[Jade Lantern]]](diagram.png)` should not create navigation edges. The parser owner explicitly documents images as non-links, the renderer leaves this alt text inert, and `linkSpans` excludes image children. An ordinary visible `[[Jade Lantern]]` must continue to create its link and backlink.

References: [shared parser and image renderer](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/blob/f6abc882721d0facb24452469b77cf58b95d25a7/extensions/knowledge/src/markdown-links.ts#L10), [navigation extraction](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/blob/f6abc882721d0facb24452469b77cf58b95d25a7/extensions/knowledge/src/markdown-links.ts#L73), [editable-link traversal](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/blob/f6abc882721d0facb24452469b77cf58b95d25a7/extensions/knowledge/src/markdown-links.ts#L157). These are derived Markdown navigation edges, not typed relationships.

### Actual behavior

Both image-alt stages return one resolved `record.links` entry and one outgoing connection. The target retains both the changing note and visible control as backlinks. All visible-link and unrelated-target controls behave correctly, and record bodies are unchanged.

| Stage | Rendered anchors / editable links | Actual note outgoing links | Actual target backlinks | Expected outgoing / backlinks |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Image alt | 0 / 0 | 1 | 2 | 0 / 1 |
| Visible wikilink | 1 / 1 | 1 | 2 | 1 / 2 |
| Image alt restored | 0 / 0 | 1 | 2 | 0 / 1 |

The shared renderer returns `<p>Fictional diagram: Caption [[Jade Lantern]]</p>` plus a newline, with no anchor. `extractLinks` nevertheless walks the image's nested tokens and collects its wikilink.

### OpenClaw version

Tested exact source `f6abc882721d0facb24452469b77cf58b95d25a7`. The full parser, unit-test, connections, renderer-consumer, and relevant documentation files are byte-identical at public main `dd1bf005936dc143b2edaf793b7bc5fef3e3e838`, checked 2026-11-08 UTC. That is file-content equivalence, not a full-repository runtime test at the newer commit. No known-good release was established.

### Operating system

Linux aarch64 (arm64), credential-free and network-isolated test namespace.

### Install method

Public source checkout with frozen dependencies, pnpm 12.15.0. Test entrypoint Node 26.13.0; the repository wrapper prepares its workers. No production plugin installation or real memory used.

### Model

Not applicable: registered-tool/native-store test, no inference call.

### Provider / routing chain

Registered Knowledge tools → native service/storage workers → link extraction/resolution. Host/session authority and all records are synthetic. The renderer observation invokes the same shared Markdown owner; no image is fetched.

### Logs

Independent replay on the pure tested base: exit 1, one file/one test failed, exactly six soft assertions (three in each image-alt stage). All three observation stages and hard controls completed. Test 5,936 ms; supported wrapper 125.87 s. This independently reproduces the original registered-tool result. No repair or fix-green is claimed.

Exact fixture SHA-256: `0fcdfcbf29f37d461cec479cd63d74f56306f9b9b2ba4c780434e4c0e913139b` (4,692 bytes).

### Screenshots, recordings, and evidence

The exact replay fixture is below. This proves registered-tool responses and shared renderer/editable-link behavior; no browser, full UI, Gateway/model, or security proof is claimed.

<details>
<summary>Standalone fictional reproduction fixture</summary>

```ts
import { randomUUID } from "node:crypto";
import type { FeatureInput, FeatureOutput } from "openclaw/plugin-sdk/feature-contract";
import type { OpenClawPluginToolFactory } from "openclaw/plugin-sdk/plugin-entry";
import { Check } from "typebox/value";
import { expect, it } from "vitest";
import { contract } from "./contract.js";
import plugin from "./index.js";
import { linkSpans, markdown } from "./markdown-links.js";
import { hostApi, sessionActions, toolContext, useTestTempDirs } from "./test-support.js";

const dirs = useTestTempDirs();
type Operation = keyof typeof contract.operations;

it("non-clickable image alt text must not create Knowledge navigation edges", async () => {
  const factories = new Map<string, OpenClawPluginToolFactory>();
  const host = hostApi(dirs.make("public-image-links-"), {
    extra: {
      ...sessionActions(),
      registerTool(factory: OpenClawPluginToolFactory, options: { name: string }) {
        factories.set(options.name, factory);
      },
    },
  });
  plugin.register(host.api);
  const context = toolContext(host.api).tool;
  async function call<K extends Operation>(operation: K, input: FeatureInput<typeof contract, K>): Promise<FeatureOutput<typeof contract, K>> {
    const tool = factories.get("knowledge_" + operation)?.(context);
    if (!tool || Array.isArray(tool)) throw new Error("Missing registered tool: " + operation);
    const result = await tool.execute(randomUUID(), input);
    const value: unknown = result.details;
    if (!Check(contract.operations[operation].output, value)) throw new Error("Invalid tool output");
    return value as FeatureOutput<typeof contract, K>;
  }
  const page = (title: string, body = "Wholly fictional project.") => call("save_page", {
    requestId: randomUUID(), type: "project", title, body,
  });
  const target = await page("Jade Lantern");
  const unrelated = await page("Copper Kite");
  const imageBody = "Fictional diagram: ![Caption [[Jade Lantern]]](diagram.png)";
  const visibleBody = "Fictional navigation: [[Jade Lantern]]";
  const note = await page("Diagram note", imageBody);
  const control = await page("Visible navigation control", visibleBody);
  for (const receipt of [target, unrelated, note, control]) expect(receipt.state).toBe("published");
  const read = () => call("record", { id: note.id, metadataView: "full" });
  async function observe(stage: string, body: string, visible: boolean) {
    const record = await read();
    expect(record.record!.body).toBe(body);
    const rendered = markdown.parse(body);
    expect(typeof rendered).toBe("string");
    const spans = linkSpans(body);
    const outgoing = await call("connections", { id: note.id, direction: "links" });
    const incoming = await call("connections", { id: target.id, direction: "backlinks" });
    const controlLinks = await call("connections", { id: control.id, direction: "links" });
    const unrelatedIncoming = await call("connections", { id: unrelated.id, direction: "backlinks" });
    expect(controlLinks.connections.map(row => row.record.id)).toEqual([target.id]);
    expect(unrelatedIncoming.connections).toEqual([]);
    expect(spans).toHaveLength(visible ? 1 : 0);
    expect(String(rendered).includes("<a ")).toBe(visible);
    const actualIds = outgoing.connections.map(row => row.record.id).sort();
    const backlinkIds = incoming.connections.map(row => row.record.id).sort();
    console.info("PUBLIC_IMAGE_LINK_PROOF", JSON.stringify({
      stage, noteId: note.id, targetId: target.id, controlId: control.id, rendered,
      spanCount: spans.length, recordLinks: record.links, outgoingIds: actualIds, backlinkIds,
      unrelatedBacklinks: unrelatedIncoming.total, controlOutgoing: controlLinks.total,
      bodyUnchanged: record.record!.body === body,
    }));
    // Soft checks preserve all opposite controls and the final round-trip stage on a red baseline.
    expect.soft(record.links).toHaveLength(visible ? 1 : 0);
    expect.soft(actualIds).toEqual(visible ? [target.id] : []);
    expect.soft(backlinkIds).toEqual((visible ? [control.id, note.id] : [control.id]).sort());
  }
  async function replaceBody(body: string) {
    const before = (await read()).record!;
    const receipt = await call("save_page", {
      requestId: randomUUID(), id: note.id, type: "project", title: "Diagram note", body,
      expectedRevision: before.revision, expectedHash: before.hash,
    });
    expect(receipt.state).toBe("published");
  }
  await observe("image-alt", imageBody, false);
  await replaceBody(visibleBody);
  await observe("visible-link", visibleBody, true);
  await replaceBody(imageBody);
  await observe("image-alt-restored", imageBody, false);
});
```

</details>

### Impact and severity

Saved or imported notes containing wikilinks inside image alt text gain phantom navigation edges. Consumers of `record.links` and links/backlinks connections receive a reference that the authored Markdown does not render as navigation. The reproduction observed no data loss, permission bypass, or production frequency.

### Additional information

A narrow repair should align navigation extraction with the existing image-rendering/editable-link contract while retaining visible links and record bytes. Current nearby Knowledge PRs were checked for path overlap; the parser and its unit test are outside those inspected slices. I am preparing a focused repair with an unchanged registered-tool replay and opposite controls. No production source edit or PR is claimed here.

