## Scope and limitations

This proves the compiled, packaged-layout OpenClaw CLI discovers and executes a real plugin command, whose calls to the compiled public SDK retain text and style offsets under an explicitly supplied numeric NaN limit. Stdout is a real local payload sink. It does **not** prove a Gateway/agent/channel-dispatch pipeline, the Zalouser transport, delivery to a recipient, or any external service. First-party limit resolution already filters NaN; this is a direct SDK/plugin-input regression, not a claim of ordinary production recipient loss. Prior unit/consumer tests cover the concrete Zalouser preparation separately.

No source changes or new commit were needed for this evidence. No runtime service was started; both CLI children and all build/copy children exited. An independent rerun of both staged CLI commands reproduced the same success/failure and checked the payload and range outputs; original PR worktree remained clean.

## What Problem This Solves

Recipients cannot consume an author's built `.tgz` directly through the native Inspect/Add workflow without manually unpacking it or publishing through ClawHub.

Closes #180518.

## Why This Change Was Made

Reuse the existing installer extractor for bounded, staged extraction and unsafe-entry rejection, then pass the extracted package to the canonical Template reader. One operation-scoped disposable source serves both Inspect and Add, keeping files alive until their effects finish.

This maintenance merge follows main's Claws-to-Templates rename in #186457. Commands, imports, types, diagnostics, tests and documentation now use the canonical Templates owner. The existing `CLAW.md` artifact name and `openclaw.template` package field remain as defined on main. No retired command alias or old reader is restored.

Existing-solutions preflight: ClawHub handles registry distribution and manual extraction remains available; neither supplies native offline archive consumption. The existing maintained archive extractor is sufficient, so no new archive engine or dependency is introduced. Current UTF-8 recovery guidance, Labs admission, selected-content identity, capability consent, dependency checks and Gateway state ownership remain in their existing owners.

## User Impact

`openclaw templates inspect ./package.tgz` and `openclaw templates add ./package.tgz` accept local `.tgz` and `.tar.gz` packages, including after the author's directory is unavailable. Directory and direct-manifest inputs remain supported.

Local archives do not acquire ClawHub trust; declared online dependencies can still require network access. Extraction is temporary and the operator's input archive is retained. No config/default, persistent source cache, database, dependency or protocol surface is added. No human acceptance of the feature is claimed by this conflict refresh.

