## What Problem This Solves

A node-bound session whose working directory matches a Gateway-local registered project or agent workspace is shown as that local project in Recents. Its execution-node identity is lost, so reopening it targets the wrong runner.

## User Impact

Remote folders keep their runner identity even when their path matches a local repository or workspace. Local sessions continue to resolve to their registered project; distinct execution nodes stay distinct.

## Why This Change Was Made

Normalize the existing node binding before implicit local-path lookup in the canonical Recents owner. Explicit project bindings, repository precedence, visibility, ordering and the eight-recent limit remain unchanged. Registered/cloned repositories and agent workspaces use this one owner; no output-by-output patching.

Existing configuration, plugins or external filtering cannot restore a node identity that the Recents projection discarded. This restores an existing binding contract. No new config/defaults, schema/protocol, security/permissions, database format or migration is introduced.

